# Keep the Docker build context (and every intermediate layer) free of
# anything that isn't needed to build the production image, per ugcportal-9rt
# acceptance criteria K2 (no dev artifacts / secrets / VCS metadata in the
# final image).
#
# THESE ARE NOT GITIGNORE PATTERNS, and the difference has already bitten
# this file. Docker matches each pattern against the whole path relative to
# the context root and `*` does not cross `/`, so a bare `*.pem` excludes
# `./key.pem` and leaves `certs/key.pem` in the context. Measured on a
# scratch context holding `top.pem` and `certs/nested.pem`: under `*.pem`
# the nested one was still in the built image, under `**/*.pem` neither was
# (ugcportal-fb32). `**/` is what makes a bare name match at every depth,
# the root included.
#
# So the name-based patterns below carry `**/`. The ones left anchored are
# anchored on purpose, for three different reasons:
#   - `.next`, `out`, `build`: `**/build` would also drop a source directory
#     called `build`. Measured: no directory of any of those three names
#     exists anywhere in this tree except `.next` at the root.
#   - `src/generated`, `.beads/embeddeddolt`, `.beads/proxieddb`,
#     `/coverage`: these name a path, not a name, so `**/` is meaningless.
#   - `.git`, `.gitignore`, `.claude`, `.codex`, `.agents`, `.github`,
#     `.runtime`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`: repo-root
#     tooling and docs. These are NOT depth-proof, and one nested copy does
#     survive into the context -- `.beads/.gitignore`. Left rather than
#     special-cased: it is beads' own ignore rules, not a secret or a dev
#     artifact, so it is outside what K2 is about. The nested AGENTS.md /
#     CLAUDE.md / CHANGELOG.md copies under `.next/standalone/` do not
#     survive, because `.next` is excluded above them.

# Dependencies (reinstalled fresh inside the image; never copy the host's)
**/node_modules
**/npm-debug.log*

# Next.js build output (rebuilt inside the image)
.next
out
build

# Generated Prisma client (regenerated inside the image from
# prisma/schema.prisma - see Dockerfile - so host state never leaks in)
src/generated

# Version control
.git
.gitignore

# Local env files / secrets — never bake these into an image layer.
#
# `**/*.pem` and not `*.pem`: `certs/capgemini.pem` is the corporate-proxy CA
# bundle docker-compose.proxy-ca.yml tells a proxied developer to create, and
# under the bare pattern it reached the build context and BOTH images.
# Measured by rebuilding both with the old pattern (PR #222 round 1):
#   builder  /app/certs/capgemini.pem  and
#            /app/.next/standalone/certs/capgemini.pem   (4334 bytes each)
#   runner   /app/certs/capgemini.pem, owned nextjs:nodejs
# The runner's copy arrives through that standalone directory: Next's
# whole-project tracing sweeps the repo into `.next/standalone`, which the
# runner stage copies wholesale. So a corporate CA bundle was being baked
# into the production image, and -- because git cannot see a gitignored
# file -- two machines produced different image contents under one pinned
# tag. See scripts/build-qa-image.sh for that second half.
**/.env
**/.env*
!.env.example
!env.example
**/*.pem
# ...and the directory docker-compose.proxy-ca.yml tells you to put the
# bundle in, by name as well: PROXY_CA_FILE accepts any path, but a bundle
# exported as `.crt`/`.cer` into `certs/` would slip past `**/*.pem`. Listing
# the directory also stops `COPY . .` leaving an empty /app/certs husk in the
# builder stage (checked both ways).
certs

# Beads issue tracker local database (large, irrelevant to the app, and
# never something that should end up in an image)
.beads/embeddeddolt
.beads/proxieddb

# Editor / OS cruft
**/.DS_Store

# Agent tooling / docs not needed at build or runtime
.claude
.codex
.agents
.github
.runtime
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
CHANGELOG.md

# Test artifacts
/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local SQLite dev databases
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
